The hardware is fine.  His problem is pilot error -- he has probably
booted from a Tru64 disk (or NetBSD, or OpenBSD, or Linux using BSD
disklabels, etc).  This can happen with the new bootstrap glue from
Mike Smith which obtains the location of / from /etc/fstab.

He needs to fix this by breaking into the boot loader & setting 
vfs.root.mountfrom to the appropriate disk.  

Somethine like 

ok set vfs.root.mountfrom=da1  

is probably what he needs.  I'm not terribly confident the
syntax is correct.

Drew

