Yoriaki FUJIMORI writes:

 > Moreover, the operating system CD cannot be read at all on all of
 > PCs and workstations in my lab.
 > 

It is UFS format, with a 512k block size.  Most CDROM readers cannot
handle this.  If you want to read it on a pc, dd the image off the
CD and mount it via vnconfig.  Also, they sometimes leave the image
"dirty", so you might need to forcibly mount it.  

