 > the official DEC/Compaq systems don't work with FreeBSD, given that
 > XFree86 has support for TGA and the *other guys* (Linux/NetBSD) can handle
 > them... 

PCI VGA cards will work, and will run XFree86.  I have personal
experiance with an S3 ViRGE based Diamond card on an AS200.  I run a
number of AS600, AS500 and my own Miata with 3D-labs based cards
(Powerstorm 4d10, as well as $30 clones).

We had somebody who was going to write TGA support, but he never
produced anything.  If TGA support is important to you, consider
writing it yourself.  The documentation is apparently readily
available (ftp://ftp.netbsd.org/pub/NetBSD/misc/dec-docs/ec-n0683-72.ps.gz)

Cheers,

Drew
