You want to install the osf1_base port.  Eg: 
cd /usr/ports/emulators/osf1_base && make && make install

The osf1 shared libraries and shared-lib loader (the /sbin/loader you
refered to above) are distributed by Compaq as part of a Netscape rpm
for alpha linux.  I don't think we are allowed to ship them
separately, so they are not included on your CDs.

I'd suggest installing the rpm port prior to installing the osf1_base
port.  The osf1_base port depends on rpm2cpio, and if you don't have
rpm installed, you'll get a painfully slow perl version of rpm2cpio..

Cheers,

Drew

